Quoting  Doug Freyburger <dfreybur@yahoo.com>:
>You value "oLS far more than I do.  I figure if I mess up enough
>to die whatever it was that I was doing isn't going to be fixed by
>a short-term second chance. 

Counting only ascensions I have records for - I have memory of one or two
more, but there is a strong selection effect there, obviously - I have 13
where I used no AoLS and 3 where I used one; in all three situations it
was not being used deliberately as a PoFH substitute. In two of those
three it was burned when the press of monsters was too great; in the first
case it was in 3.1.3 and I could not have used a PoFH instead because they
didn't exist, and in the second case I had burned all my PoFH which was
clearly an error. Only in the third case was it an unforeseen instakill -
poison - and in that case it was not a stupid-typo death.

Furthermore for 11 of those 13 I have records about my wearing of AoLS. In
7 cases I was wearing it at ascension time; in one of those there is a
note that I wore it only on the Astral plane. In an 8th case there is a
note that I would have worn it but forgot to. In 2 of the 3 cases where I
am not wearing one, there is a note that I never wore it. In one of those
2 cases, I was using the amulet slot for reflection; in the other one and
in the aforementioned 7th case, I obviously preferred ESP.

Furthermore the 3 ascensions where I used an AoLS are my 1st, 9th, and
12th of 22 total.

That suggests to me that it certainly is possible to be lifesaved once but
then to recover the situation; that this is considerably less likely with
the introduction of the PoFH (given that sensible use of PoFH would
salvage the situation); that the time to be wearing AoLS is in the early
game when PoFH are not available, deaths such as poison or massive mumak
damage are more likely, and other valuable amulets are less likely to be
available (but even with, say, AoESP available, an AoLS may be better);
and that a more experienced player who can make better use of other
amulets is less likely to benefit from AoLS.

Unfortunately, what I obviously don't have figures on are the number of
games where I died but would have ascended had I had an AoLS.
